  "id": "COMPOUND:16359 - PROTEIN:6340",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Opacaline B may interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through a series of target relationships. Specifically, Opacaline B is directly linked to DMS-79, which in turn is a target of two different compounds—32,33-dihydro-31-hydroxymanzamine A and Phlorofucofuroeckol A. Both of these compounds are predicted to target the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, indicating that Opacaline B may share a common pathway of action with these compounds. The consistent scores across the three paths (final_score=0.5695) suggest a potential functional relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear. The evidence supports the possibility that Opacaline B modulates the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, possibly through the inhibition of its enzymatic activity or by influencing its subunit composition. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of DMS-79 as a central mediator in the interaction network, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct involvement of Opacaline B in this process.",
